      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 7060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-07-23T18:15:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "signing and encryption keys are the result of a derivation, we store a service key encrypted in a master key.\nIf we stored signing and encryption key we would never be able to add different derivations in the future, this is why generally in cryptography they are always computed at time of use and not stored.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAQn//0KM\u003d",
